Passage: REG, Annex III, 4.3.1

[0] 4.3.1.
[1] Chains, ropes and webbing Each length of lifting chain, rope or webbing not forming part of an assembly shall bear a mark or, where this is not possible, a plate or irremovable ring bearing the name and address of the manufacturer and the identifying reference of the relevant certificate.
[2] The certificate mentioned above shall show at least the following information:
[3] (a) the name and address of the manufacturer;
[4] (b) a description of the chain or rope, which includes:
[5] (i) its nominal size;
[6] (ii) its construction;
[7] (iii) the material from which it is made;
[8] and (iv) any special metallurgical treatment applied to the material;
[9] (c) the test method used;
[10] (d) the maximum load to which the chain or rope should be subjected in service.
[11] A range of values may be given on the basis of the intended applications.
